// ROUND30 P1 corrective suite — regression tests for the two independently reported P1 defects (PR #4 @ 5f928e2):
//   P1-A  a required signer's domain authority changed between the pre-transaction checks and the PREPARE batch, yet a
//         PREPARED package was committed (SQL only re-checked active membership, not signoff-domain eligibility).
//   P1-B  an identical lot-opening retry with the same Idempotency-Key returned 500 instead of replaying the success.
// Real Worker HTTP handler + real SQLite engine through the D1 adapter (batch() = BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK). The commit
// window is the moment after every JavaScript read of the request and immediately before env.DB.batch() runs: a hook
// there commits a competing write (role/membership/signoff/release change) exactly where the TOCTOU lives.
// Every row prints a MATRIX line (matrix, id, scenario, expected, actual, verdict) consumed by the QA evidence CSVs.
